\title{MIR text marks record references with a sigil}
\taxon{Change}
\date{2026-11-13}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{changelog}
\tag{compiler-runtime}
\tag{unreleased}
\meta{release}{Unreleased}
\meta{pr}{987}
\import{base-macros}

\p{A record reference in textual MIR is written \code{\verb~|#path~}, as in textual HIR. A record named after a builtin type, such as \code{\verb~|Ptr~}, \code{\verb~|Tensor~}, \code{\verb~|Arc~} or \code{\verb~|Token~}, used to parse back as that type or not at all. Hand-written MIR must add the sigil. \pr{987}.}
